    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7b9",
      "function_role": "altered-dominant-spice",
      "narrative": "Greene classifies dom7b9 as an 'altered dominant' \u2014 'those with #9's, b9's, #5's, and b5's,' calling them 'very spicy chords' (Ch.11, p.78). For III7-VI7-II7-V7 progressions, use altered dominants including dom7b9 on any position to create chromatic intensity.",
