      "narrative": "Ch.11 (p.78) substitution rule runs both directions: where a III7 or VI7 altered dominant appears, one may substitute the diatonic version \u2014 'try using iii7 types in place of III7 types, or vi7 types in place of VI7 types.' Dom7alt is not mandatory; diatonic min7 substitution always available as softening option.",
